--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/decisions/2026-11-02-tensor-layout-error.md
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+# Classify tensor-layout mismatches without claiming corruption
+
+An Ollama model matched its full SHA-256 digest but llama.cpp b11946 rejected it with "wrong number of tensors; expected 1189, got 833". A tensor count mismatch alone is therefore not evidence of damaged bytes.
+
+Classify this message as MODEL_ARCH_NOT_SUPPORTED for upstream llama.cpp as well as the fork. Explicit truncation, invalid magic, and end-of-file markers remain MODEL_FILE_CORRUPT. Keep original desktop fixtures unchanged and document the intentional contract correction in the test.
